id: pm-o3fh
title: Repair calendar shortcut package discovery and upgrade migration guidance
description: "The three calendar shortcut commands become builtin-calendar package-owned commands (or pm create --template sugar), removing 3 top-level core entries while keeping every flag; core keeps alias shims while the deprecation cycle runs. Duplicate check: PR#263 shipped the shortcuts; pm-ixoa is a calendar service collision, different concern."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:extensions",calendar,simplification
created_at: "2026-07-05T04:53:33.905Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-22T07:04:25.109Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-22T07:04:24.226Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-22T07:04:24.226Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: meet/event/remind live in builtin-calendar (package-owned commands) with full flag parity incl. scheduling presets and relative-time parsing; core alias shims keep old spellings working; uninstalling the package surfaces the owning-package hint (pm-b3e9 pattern); calendar shortcut specs pass via aliases
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Package-owned calendar aliases now recover with canonical installation and help guidance; CLI upgrade receipts expose optional migration guidance, and synchronous version lookup has no redundant await."
expected_result: Clear missing-package recovery and statically valid SDK upgrade execution without changing existing scheduling behavior.
actual_result: Real CLI recovery/install tests and the 698-test changed-boundary suite pass with exact 100-percent coverage in all four dimensions. ESLint and SDK signatures pass; final hosted checks and external review remain required for merge.
