comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T03:12:04.056Z","harness:codex","Verification: linked package/core registration tests passed; 53 runtime contract tests passed; typecheck and ESLint passed; generated contracts and agent surfaces refreshed with zero SDK export changes. Manual disposable Node and Bun sessions passed install, missing-package recovery, aliases, 5min persistence, rejected update atomicity, month-end clamping, reminders, doctor, validation, and uninstall. Packed npm/npx/bunx smoke passed. Static gate identified automation-guide routing drift; canonical guide examples are being corrected before the final full gate."
  "2026-09-18T03:14:37.176Z","harness:codex","Independent live checks 2026-09-18: GitHub open PRs and Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning alerts were empty; GH-1246 already has the canonical pm-z3ez item link. Last scheduled Auto Release run 35197095403 succeeded and v2026.9.17 is public on GitHub and npm. The workflow serializes automatic runs and verifies an existing same-day immutable tag before preparation. Sentry/telemetry required-mode gate passed: zero critical/high unresolved issues, 1.11 percent weighted finish error rate, zero failure rows missing error codes. Live database had 508 events in the previous hour and a fresh timestamp; RabbitMQ had zero queued or unacknowledged messages."
  "2026-09-18T03:14:38.165Z","harness:codex","All-status graph verification: 2768 recorded nodes and 13824 directed edges form one connected knowledge component with zero orphans and no ordering or hierarchy cycles. Execution has 12 layers and critical path length 11. Seven grandfathered hierarchy cardinality/direction records remain informational; no active hierarchy violations. New duration lineage uses implements, discovered_from, and verifies edges rather than adding associative links to inflate counts. Only pm-o3fh and pm-jkjt are currently in progress."
  "2026-09-18T03:20:50.653Z","harness:codex","Full-suite first pass: 8972 passed and 10 failures exposed stale registration/alias assertions, strict sandbox profile inconsistent with declared writes, help budget inventory dropping migrated commands, and guide routing against the prior build. Correcting production integration and contract observations; no budget increases or coverage exclusions."
  "2026-09-18T03:30:25.413Z","harness:codex","Migration gate fixes now pass focused tests (49 tests): full nested guide routing, retained calendar help budgets, and real installed package contracts. Pure command metadata is separated from SDK execution bindings so native Node gate imports do not need a workspace package self-link. In-process package SDK dispatch also verifies all three default scheduling handlers against persisted items."
  "2026-09-18T03:42:17.526Z","harness:codex","Final integration checks: package artifact smoke passed again after the metadata/runtime split; live telemetry flush drained the queue to zero. Static quality, docstrings, duplication, package/SDK parity, grammar, help budgets, refusal closure, agent-token gates, tracker-context quality, gate registry, and SDK snapshot checks passed. Import-cost checks initially exceeded budgets under simultaneous coverage load, then SDK and transport benchmarks passed after that load ended without changing limits. Validation retains the documented 170 unrecoverable historical resolution gaps; individual active histories match their latest records."
  "2026-09-18T03:55:48.309Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: 705 test files and 8,984 tests passed; statement coverage 64,769/64,769, branch coverage 49,414/49,414, function coverage 13,443/13,443 and line coverage 61,995/61,995, all 100%. No coverage exclusions or thresholds were added or relaxed. Linked pm tests passed. TypeScript, ESLint, zero-clone duplication scans, 100% source/export/member docstring gates, contracts, SDK parity, generated surfaces, guide routing and existing help budgets passed. All static stages passed; unchanged SDK import-cost and CLI transport budgets were rerun successfully without concurrent coverage load. Temporary Node and Bun manual sessions verified install/uninstall recovery, canonical and legacy scheduling, atomic refusal and calendar-month clamping. Packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance passed. Secret scan and dependency audit passed. Current GitHub security-alert inventories were empty. Sentry required gate passed with no unresolved issues; telemetry delivery drained the queue. Hosted PR checks and external reviews follow this local evidence and are independent claims."
  "2026-09-22T05:46:10.285Z","harness:codex","Evidence: red tests reproduced missing package recovery and missing upgrade guidance. The repaired real CLI passes text and JSON missing-command diagnostics, project package installation, and legacy help retry; 141 focused tests pass. SDK migration_guidance is an optional additive receipt field. No optional workflow is automatically installed."
  "2026-09-22T06:04:35.824Z","harness:codex","Coverage evidence: 698 focused CLI, upgrade, release-generator and integration tests pass. Across the three changed behavior files, V8 reports statements 584/584, branches 513/513, functions 120/120 and lines 568/568. General help remains available alongside the preferred owning-package install and canonical command examples."
  "2026-09-22T06:27:26.994Z","harness:codex",The two original linked commands retain provenance from the earlier delivery branch and were correctly refused by current-branch trust checks. Their sandboxed runner commands have been reviewed and are being re-registered unchanged under this active delivery; no trust or lock override is used. The new recovery test already passed via pm test.
  "2026-09-22T06:33:43.235Z","harness:codex","Delivery verification: the new linked recovery suite passed 141 tests, including real absent-package text/JSON diagnostics, installation, and legacy help retry. Packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance passed across nine packages; the additive optional SDK receipt field is captured in the public snapshot. The two original sandboxed command links remain present with reviewed current-branch provenance; a duplicate release-note test link was removed from its owning issue so the same suite is not registered twice."
  "2026-09-22T06:43:30.791Z","harness:codex","Final repository coverage passed: 725 files and 9192 tests; statements 64834/64834, branches 49506/49506, functions 13467/13467, lines 62037/62037. All exact thresholds remain 100 percent. Typecheck, ESLint, zero-clone scans, 100-percent module/export/member documentation, structural/static contracts, graph composition and record integrity passed. Temporary Node/Bun lifecycle and packed npm/npx/bunx consumers passed. Local import/transport timing is documented separately because unchanged main also exceeds budgets on this host; hosted gates and reviews are still required before merge."
  "2026-09-22T06:48:40.024Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1286 — command-domain organization, mandatory private-export gate, package recovery and complete release evidence. Source implementation and local verification are committed; exact-head hosted checks and external review determine merge readiness."
  "2026-09-22T07:02:01.214Z","harness:codex","DeepScan exact-head finding 235039259 on PR 1286: removing the one-use async version wrapper left await on synchronous resolvePmCliVersion(), whose declared return is string or undefined. Remove that await and rerun upgrade/CLI coverage. Report: https://deepscan.io/dashboard/#view=project&tid=30234&pid=32092&bid=1075618&iid=235039259. Chrome Computer Use was unavailable in this session; the public provider API supplied the exact commit, file, line and rule."
  "2026-09-22T07:04:23.477Z","harness:codex","Review correction verified: removed the unnecessary await from synchronous resolvePmCliVersion. The 698-test changed-boundary suite passes with exact coverage 584/584 statements, 513/513 branches, 120/120 functions and 568/568 lines; ESLint and the public SDK snapshot pass. On the prior PR head, all hosted checks except DeepScan passed, including full coverage and the unchanged performance budgets. CodeRabbit declined the file count, Sourcery could not fetch the large diff, and Codex reported an unavailable GitHub connection; these are unavailable review evidence, not approvals. A new exact-head review/check round follows the fix."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T03:03:54.634Z","harness:codex","Architecture: calendar extension declares commands and flags over public SDK functions; generic SDK/MCP operation identities stay native. Core bootstrap retains legacy alias rewriting and missing-package recovery. Contract discovery distinguishes callable SDK actions from installed CLI commands."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T03:03:55.471Z","harness:codex","Host-owned global flags such as --author must not be registered by packages: extension activation rejects collisions. Real installed-package tests verify global identity forwarding and persisted history rather than mocking the registration layer."
  "2026-09-18T03:27:27.047Z","harness:codex",Package relocation must preserve the independent help budget inventory and full command-path documentation routing; a gate that matches only the root verb can silently lose or falsely reject nested capabilities. Keep negative controls for omitted package registration and parent/sibling confusion.
